            <ArticleTitle>Transient left posterior hemiblock during Prinzmetal's angina culminating in acute myocardial infarction.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>638-40</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 49-year-old man had transient left posterior hemiblock during Prinzmetal's angina with inferior ST-segment elevations; subsequently, left posterior hemiblock reappeared associated with acute inferior myocardial infarction. The electrocardiographic and electrophysiologic aspects of these findings are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
